{"notes":["# Security Review — sto:local-deploy-config @149e39d / fcac70c\n\n**Verdict: NOT BLOCKING — PASS with notes (sec-approve with follow-ups).** No prod MITM bypass, secrets redacted, input validation solid. 2 medium / 3 low findings, all non-blocking for this STO scope.\n\n## Scope\n- Commit fcac70c: server.targets[env] single-source (ADR-005), host-key verification, DEPLOY_SSH_KEY override + ssh-agent, redaction\n- Files: internal/config/server.go + loader.go + defaults.go, internal/deployment/ssh_credentials.go + ssh_transport.go, internal/output/redact.go, cmd/deploy.go\n\n## AC Coverage\n- AC1 ✅ host/user/ip validation (ValidateHost net.ParseIP+RFC1123 regex, ValidateUser POSIX regex, port 1-65535)\n- AC2 ✅ prod guards enforced in both ValidateServerTarget (config validate) and ResolveSSHCredentialsForTarget (runtime): prod/production require KnownHostsPath, reject accept-new (TOFU) → strict only\n- AC3 ✅ DEPLOY_SSH_KEY override via EffectiveSSHKeyPath (TrimSpace env wins), empty → ssh-agent preferred via SSH_AUTH_SOCK + PublicKeysCallback; redaction via SanitizeLogLine+RedactSecrets\n- AC4 ✅ ValidateServerTargetsInFlat integrated into LoadConfig/ResolveAndValidateConfig; framework-free (no server section) tolerated\n\n## Findings\n### MEDIUM-1: InsecureIgnoreHostKey remains default for non-prod (exposure window)\n- Where: internal/deployment/ssh_transport.go:374-376 hostKeyCallback() returns ssh.InsecureIgnoreHostKey() when KnownHostsPath==\"\"\n- Impact: MITM on staging/dev if DNS hijack. Documented as legacy TD-004 opt-in, prod blocked by dual guards. Acceptable for MVP.\n- Evidence: dial with empty knownHosts still succeeds (TestSSHTransport_Deliver_NoKnownHosts_AcceptsAnyKey). Non-prod not rejected.\n- Mitig: Ensure runbook/docs recommend knownHostsPath even for staging; consider warning log when KnownHostsPath empty + !framework-free; plan to flip default to strict in next epic.\n\n### MEDIUM-2: Private key file permissions not enforced\n- Where: internal/deployment/ssh_transport.go:295 loadSigner os.ReadFile(KeyPath) no mode check; key created in tests as 0600 but prod key could be 0644/0666\n- Impact: world-readable key on shared runner leaks via filesystem.\n- Mitig: Add pre-flight warning if file mode \u0026 0o077 !=0 (log sanitized), and/or chmod 0600 guidance in docs. Not blocking — key content never logged (redacted).\n\n### LOW-1: known_hosts accept-new symlink append risk\n- Where: ssh_transport.go:437 os.OpenFile(KnownHostsPath, O_APPEND|O_CREATE|O_WRONLY, 0600) without O_NOFOLLOW\n- Impact: If KnownHostsPath attacker-controlled via anvil.yaml symlink, could append to arbitrary file. Operator-controlled config in this threat model; not exploitable via user input.\n- Mitig: Add O_NOFOLLOW + lstat check or document that path must be regular file owned by operator.\n\n### LOW-2: DEPLOY_SSH_KEY content-vs-path confusion + log surface\n- Where: internal/config/server.go:414 EffectiveSSHKeyPath trusts env verbatim; ssh_transport.go:297 error includes KeyPath %q\n- Impact: If operator mistakenly sets DEPLOY_SSH_KEY to PEM content (common), path becomes multi-line secret. Mitigated: SanitizeLogLine in cmd/deploy.go redacts DEPLOY_SSH_KEY value and \"private/begin open\" → ***REDACTED***, but ssh_transport auth errors bypass deploy.go sanitizer (return as TransportError). Low likelihood.\n- Mitig: In EffectiveSSHKeyPath/authMethods, reject value containing newline or \"-----BEGIN\" with clear error before file read.\n\n### LOW-3: Agent socket FD leak\n- Where: ssh_transport.go:322 net.Dial(\"unix\", sock) stored in agent.NewClient(conn) callback, never Close()\n- Impact: FD leak per dial; not security-exploitable, but long-lived process could exhaust.\n- Mitig: Defer conn.Close() after dialWithAuth or wrap in closer tied to ssh.Client lifetime.\n\n## Positive Controls Observed\n- ValidateHost correctly rejects dotted-numeric invalid IP (isDottedNumeric → net.ParseIP gate, e.g. 999.999.999.999)\n- ValidateUser length 32, regex anchored, empty rejected\n- validateRemotePath blocks shell metachars before any dial (defense in depth, tested with Connections()==0)\n- hostKeyCallback fail-closed: strict rejects unknown/changed, accept-new rejects changed key (KeyError Want!=0), missing file in strict → KindConfiguration before dial\n- recordHostKey with 0600\n- SanitizeLogLine replaces env values verbatim + path redaction + private marker; used in deploy.go error+warning paths so JSON envelope stays clean\n- Prod guard duplicated in config validation and runtime credential resolve (defense in depth)\n\n## Secrets Handling ✓\n- DEPLOY_SSH_KEY value redacted via SanitizeLogLine before any user-facing output (deploy.go:188,191,193). RedactSecrets covers key paths/id_rsa/.pem. No raw key content logged. Tests confirm PASS.\n\n## Recommendation\n- Ship fcac70c. Track follow-ups: staging known_hosts warning, key perm check, O_NOFOLLOW, PEM-in-env guard, agent conn close. None block prod.\n\nReviewer: alex-security (M2Code) — 2026-08-25\nCommit: fcac70c (sto:local-deploy-config:1 149e39d)"],"role":"review","verdict":"approve"}